--- body ---
## Context

The JET Grants Register (South Africa, Presidential Climate Commission /
JET PMU) is a repeated series: one register per period, same columns. Four
editions are held, all pending (a snapshot, no line):

| Document | Format |
|---|---|
| `zaf-jet-grants-register-2023-q3` (JET-IP Grant Mapping Register) | PDF, 31 pages, one wide table with wrapped cells |
| `zaf-jet-grants-register-2024-q2` | PDF |
| `zaf-jet-grants-register-2024-q3` | XLSX |
| `zaf-jet-grants-register-2025-q1` | XLSX |

Why a parser: extraction § 6.1 gives a repeated series a parser, not
assisted reading. Measured 2026-10-01:

- Panel v1 ([[1895]]): on the 2023-q3 PDF, GLM-5.3 lost 138 of 140 rows to
  locators, GPT-5.6 60 of 140; the South African table-row stratum rests
  on that one document.
- Docling ([[1940]] log): 29 page tables with real cells, but each
  continuation page's first row becomes a header (about 28 rows) and some
  rows merge, about 100 clean rows against 157 US dollar amounts in the
  text layer.

The columns, as printed in 2023-q3: Priority Area, Priority Areas
(Description), Purpose, Source Group, Activities - Descriptions,
Implementing institution, Funder, Funding instrument, Total US$, Total ZAR,
Source, Parties to the funding agreement(s), Other key beneficiaries, Key
terms and conditions, Disbursements status, Status - Dynamic, % Completed,
Detailed Descriptions, Start Date, End Date; with a USD-to-ZAR rate
printed on the first page.

## Method

- XLSX editions first: cells as stored, sheet by sheet, hidden rows and
  sheets read and marked (extraction § 5). Locator: sheet and row.
- PDF editions: a cell-level reader (pdfplumber, or Docling's table output
  with the continuation-header and merged-row defects repaired), checked
  row by row against the printed totals and, where an XLSX edition repeats
  a grant, against it. Locator: page, table and row.
- Each row is one statement (`register_allocation` unless the register
  presents it otherwise); the column headers as printed are the verbatim
  fields, under a declared, versioned header mapping per edition; the
  publisher's status words copied as printed (`own_status`), no axis.
- The exchange-rate note on the first page is a heading statement that
  governs the rows.
- Lines written through the ledger writers (`_ledger_headers.write_table`),
  under a named parser method and version.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Parser for the series reads all four editions; a document it cannot
  read fails whole (extraction § 6.1), never partly
- [ ] Tests on fixtures drawn from the real snapshots, red-tested with at
  least: a shifted grid, a missing page or sheet, a duplicated row, a
  count or total that disagrees with the printed one (extraction § 12)
- [ ] Row counts per edition reported and reconciled with printed totals;
  the 2023-q3 PDF reconciled with the 157 US dollar amounts of its text
  layer (each amount accounted for, or the reason it is not a row)
- [ ] Lines admitted under the parser's method and version; the four
  editions leave the pending list
- [ ] `make check-fast` and `make lint` pass
